From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:11:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/27] flashnext: prompt passes native read-out runs as two
 fused kernels and the shared output reads in place

A prompt pass native hyper-connection read-out (TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_HC2=1, from TF_FLASHNEXT_HC2_MIN
rows) runs on the hcn kernels in flashnext_hcf.cu: the norm formed in the down tile shared memory and
the up rows mixed in the up kernel epilogue, every output byte the five-launch chain (tests/cuda
hc-fuse). The MoE write-back reads the shared expert fp32 output in place
(TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_SHARED_DIRECT=1) instead of a copy of it in y last slot, and a prompt chunk MTP
head pass takes at most TF_FLASHNEXT_HEAD_PIECE rows (256, the decode rounds piece).
